// (10 Qs), Domain 4 Regulatory Compliance 20% (20 Qs), Domain 5 Information
// Technologies 10% (10 Qs) — midpoints of each domain's official percentage
// range. 100 questions total (real exam is 107: 97 scored + 10 unscored
// pretest; 100 is a clean round practice-paper length close to the real
// scored count). Every question tests durable coding LOGIC/GUIDELINES
// (UHDDS rules, ICD-10-PCS root-operation definitions, POA indicator
// meaning, sequencing principles, query-compliance rules, HIPAA/PSI/HAC
// concepts) rather than specific numeric code lookups that date quickly or
// require the exact current codebook to verify — same approach used for
// AWS SAA (stable service behavior over volatile pricing/console details).
// SOURCE: authored from AHIMA's published CCS Exam Content Outline and
// standard, stable coding-guideline knowledge (ICD-10-CM/PCS Official
// Guidelines, UHDDS, CMS POA guidance) — not copied from any official AHIMA
// exam question bank, which AHIMA does not publish.

